A||N||9||GT-maniac||Supply of 2.8L V6's as used in the fiero ?||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||09-15-2000||10:51 AM||||Hi guys I'm looking for the same hi output 2.8 that's used in the fiero and need alternative cars to search for. Fiero's in the wreckers are pretty much non existant in my area. 85 - 87 camaro's maybe ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-15-2000||11:04 AM||||I'm not sure but I think they used the H.O. in Cavaleir Z-24's. If you want you can get a 3.1 from Grand Prix's, Regal's, Early 90's Z-24, Lumina's, Cutlass', ETC that would be an easy swap. I think the 3.1's were rated at 150-160hp. If you go with a 3.1 you can use all the external parts from your 2.8 (Manifolds, distributor, brackets, etc)<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||whamel||09-15-2000||11:06 AM||||Do you happen to know which years?  I looked at the Z-24 and was concerned that the one I saw had a different power rating than the 2.8 in the Fiero.  I don't know Cavalier's though at all.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>I'm not sure but I know they used the H.O. in Cavaleir Z-24's. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sarlacc||09-15-2000||12:28 PM||||I believe that the 60 degree's in most of the FWD cars mentioned use aluminum heads.  That would make it a bit more complicated to swap over the Fiero parts since you would need to swap heads too (and install different pistons).  I cannot see why one would want to swap the Fiero parts at all unless they needed to keep it original looking for some reason?  I tried to spur some conversation on how best to swap in the FWD 60 degree aluminum head motors and still use the Fiero computer (Minivan vs Camaro thread) , but there really does not seem to be much interest in this.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-15-2000||01:51 PM||||The Fiero computer pretty much requires a distributor. The aluminum head motors use DIS, instead of a distributor. The intake manifold configuration prevents the installation of a distributor. I don't know if the Fiero computer can be modded to talk to a DIS system, but I suspect that it would be easier to just swap in the one that belongs with the engine.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sarlacc||09-15-2000||04:34 PM||||The retrofit to DIS is about as complicated as splicing in a different plug "if you have a crank sensor".  The DIS module determines the timing and spark based on the crank sensor, and will interface to the Fiero computer exactly the same as the distributor system does.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||09-15-2000||04:58 PM||||Sarlacc, is this something that you have done, already?<BR>I suspect that a lot of folks haven't tried this because it is quite intimidating.<P>There also is the issue of batch firing injectors vs. sequential. I've heard that with no other changes, SFI offers better "part throttle " response and fuel economy.  <P>This is all stuff that I've read. Mostly on this Forum. Don't claim to know for sure.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sarlacc||09-15-2000||08:10 PM||||Sure, I can give you any info you need on this.  Here are the pinouts for the two different systems<P>Fiero 2.8 (plug located on ignition control module mounted in distributor)<P>A -- WHT  --------- EST<BR>B -- PPL/WHT ------ REFERENCE PULSE HIGH<BR>C -- TAN/BLK ------ BY-PASS<BR>D -- BLK/RED ------ REFERENCE PULSE LOW<P>3100,3400 V6 DIS system (plug located on  coil pack, ignition control module is mounted under coil pack) <P>A -- WHT  --------- TACHOMETER<BR>B -- PPL/WHT ------ REFERENCE PULSE HIGH<BR>C -- EMPTY  ------- NOT USED<BR>D -- BLK/RED ------ REFERENCE PULSE LOW<BR>E -- TAN/BLK ------ BY-PASS<BR>F -- WHT  --------- EST<P>As you can see, it is simply a matter of splicing the wires from the Fiero ignition control module plug into the new DIS module plug. The color codes are exactly the same, the wires just enter the two plugs at different locations.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||09-15-2000||11:09 PM||||DOH!!!<BR>Well, cool!<BR>Sounds like a case of "been there, done that". <P>I guess that I had assumed (there's that word) that since the 87 and 88 4 cylinder used a "new" (reportedly smarter) ECM when they switched to DIS, that there was some smoke, mirrors, and voodoo (or at least another pile of electronics) involved.<P>I suspect that 3.4 swaps are about third on the list of most popular topics, right behind clutch repair and brake upgrades. <BR>Oh yeah, and Pine Tree air fresheners.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cooter||09-15-2000||11:39 PM||||TerryK- is that all there is to making a DIS motor work on a Fiero ECM?||||reg||1
